L0202: Duplicate declaration or field

Two declarations introduce the same name in a namespace that requires uniqueness, or two fields repeat a label. A let binding may shadow a previous let, but declaration and field lists are not shadowing scopes. Rename or remove the duplicate.

Example from `tests/corpus/reject/duplicate_field.lc`; the full file is a regression test.

```locus
// Two fields with one name, in a struct and in a tuple type.
struct Lock {
    failures: u8,
    failures: u8,
}

fn pair(n: u8) -> (out: u8, out: u8) {
    (n, n)
}
```

Language, as built: [1.2:1](../../atlas.html#/doc/language/spec-1.2:1).
